James sought to improve a paragraph in his report on climate adaptation actions, addressing feedback that it mixed various adaptation types. He requested a rewrite that distinguishes between reactive and planned adaptations. In response, I provided a revised paragraph that clarified the two categories: reactive adaptations, like household cooling during heatwaves, and planned adaptations, such as coastal defenses and soil management. The rewrite emphasized that planned actions necessitate extensive planning and capital investment while also noting their broader impacts on ecosystems and communities.
